# The Dockerfile whitelists what it copies (see the COPY block in the env
# stage), so this file is no longer the primary defense against junk in the
# image — it only has to exclude things living INSIDE the whitelisted
# directories. Adding a new top-level directory to the image is a Dockerfile
# change, not a change here.

# Frontend deps, inside aiarena/frontend-spa/. The build output Django actually
# serves is aiarena/frontend-spa/static/dist, which is produced before the image
# build and deliberately NOT excluded.
#
# Must be `**/node_modules`: a bare `node_modules` only matches at the context
# root, which is why the old entry never excluded the SPA's copy.
**/node_modules

# Python bytecode and caches
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
